Roles and responsibilites of software engineers
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

   Primary Responsibilites of entry level software engineer:

      1. Developing solutions.
      2. Testing and finalsing solution
      3. Fixing errors
      4. Coordinating and communicating with a team and other stakeholders.
      5. Learning and teaching new technologies and skills.

1. Developing solutions
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
        * Understand the task that is being asked of you.
        * Review existing documentation on the topic.
        * Ask questions as needed to clarify task.
        * use coding best practices
        * code needed for solution
        * resue code when appropriate.

2. Testing and finalising solutions
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
        * Use a DevOps approach to make code reviews along coding process
        * have knowledge of willing to self-teach about tests (eg: Unit testing)
        * Track code production (e.g APM(Automatic Project Management) or (Application Performance Management) TO Track systems and discover error)
        * Test solutions across different softwares.

3. Fixing errors
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
         * Locate the code that contains error independently or with support colleagues.
         * Test the functionality that has error (Runtime error)
         * Understand the techincal details of the current error
         * Test that solution is working correctly
         * Test everything that can be affected by the error (whole system).

4. Coordinating and communicating with a team and other stakeholders:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 
         * Participate in and organise team discuusions (eg: Sprint Planning, Daily Scrum, sprint retrospective)
         * Use team meetings as an opportunity to raise questions and problema(concerning yoour own / other's work)
         * Define situations in which it is accectable to reach out to a collegaue for a help vs independent problem-solvimg
         * Find trusted contact persons who are willing to help
         * Identify desired ways of support provided by selected contact persons(eg pair programming, online chat tools like slack,reviews on Github, etc).

5. Learning and teaching new technologies and skiills.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

         * Have knowledge of/be willing self-teach about programming language (object-oriented & functional development ) and any other needed tool.


